# Chart intent + next-RTH residual language (RC-163)

Failure modes: (1) claiming Collect / accrual ACCEPT/CLOSED/Done while Chart render
(yellow bars / GEX bars / paint) stays OUT-OF-SCOPE or soft OBSERVED with no open
P0/CHART_CONSUMER residual; (2) writing "Monday proof" when next RTH is not Monday.

## Laws

1. **Chart intent is product delivery.** Accumulate-and-render is not Done when only the
   bank landed. Finish language for Collect/accrual/bank requires a proven Chart consumer,
   or explicit `STATUS PARTIAL` naming an open Chart residual (`P0` / `CHART_CONSUMER`).
2. **Escape:** `# chart-intent-ok:` + operator waiver (Collect-only carve-out).
3. **Next-RTH calendar honesty.** Before any forward residual uses a weekday name, compute
   next RTH with `time_et.is_trading_day_et` (America/New_York) and state **ISO date +
   weekday**. Prefer `NEXT_RTH_PROOF` + that date over inherited `MONDAY_PROOF` labels.
4. **Escape:** `# next-rth-ok:` with the explicit computed date. Do not rename historical
   gate files (`gex_r1_monday_collector_gate*`) — only fix forward residual language you touch.

## Soft (not machine-locked — NLP hell)

- "one viewport" Done without a two-viewport mention
- treating "freeze without live volume" as Chart proof

## Enforcers

- `check_chart_intent_and_next_rth` in `tools/check_institutional_correctness.py` (enforced check; since RC-406 the catalog runs in required CI — `.github/workflows/hardening.yml` — on every PR, not at commit)
- `tools/pretooluse_guard.py` + `tools/chart_intent_lock.py` (Edit/Write BLOCK on residual /
  handoff / RC / prompt paths)
